{"type":"text","timestamp":1791296875873,"sessionID":"ses_eee64f166ffetKE5aG292H35oH","part":{"id":"prt_1119d28ca001RNQUNgXyTL1Dl1","messageID":"msg_1119d1e3c001UMVLGha6ckVDSR","sessionID":"ses_eee64f166ffetKE5aG292H35oH","type":"text","text":"6/6 tests pass, and all documented edge cases verified (negative formats like `-$0.05`, `'0.5'` → 50, month/day ordering, tie-breaks, default `n=3`).\n\nBugs fixed:\n\n1. `ledger/money.py` — `format_cents` broke on negatives: floor division/modulo on negative cents gave `-$-4.90` for `-310`. Now it uses `abs()` before dividing.\n2. `ledger/parse.py` — `parse_date` returned `(year, day, month)` with month and day swapped. Now it returns `(year, month, day)`.\n3. `ledger/report.py` — `top_items` sorted totals ascending and returned the n smallest, and ignored the tie rule. Now it sorts by total descending, ties by item name ascending.","time":{"start":1791296874698,"end":1791296875857}}}
